{
  "evidence": "TEXT_D: 10,000 more police and completion of 20,000 CSOs; creation of a UK Border Force; protect jury trial with tighter judicial oversight and intercept evidence; maintain a minimum nuclear deterrent while pursuing multilateral disarmament; prisons focused on work/skills with progress tied to effort; free personal care for elderly/disabled, abolition of tuition fees, expanded NHS exemptions and mental health rights; Single Equality Act and hate‑crime units; carbon tax and cleaner‑energy incentives; War Powers and Civil Service Acts with stronger parliamentary scrutiny. TEXT_C: Decommission nuclear weapons and cut defence to EU average; universal non‑means‑tested Citizen’s Income and Citizen’s Pension; steeply more progressive taxation and shift to eco‑taxes; public ownership of rail/Tube and re‑regulation of buses; zero‑waste bans (including incineration), ban GM food, extensive animal‑welfare prohibitions; oppose EU constitution, disestablish the state church, limit the monarchy, local recall/referenda and fully elected upper chamber.",
  "reasoning": "Given a profile that prioritises Authority and Care (with moderate Loyalty and Proportionality), TEXT_D better matches these weights by reinforcing policing, borders, nuclear deterrence and rule‑of‑law safeguards (authority/loyalty) alongside substantial but targeted social care and health commitments, and effort‑linked rehabilitation (proportionality). TEXT_C emphasises lower‑priority foundations for this profile—strong equality and sanctity (citizen’s income, sweeping redistribution, zero‑waste/GM bans) and subversion of traditional authorities (decommissioning nukes, cutting defence, disestablishing the church/limiting the monarchy).",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_D"
}
